10
00:54:17,142 --> 00:54:23,142
Elizabeth: The Golden Age is a 2007 biographical historical drama film directed by
Shekhar Kapur and produced by Universal Pictures and Working Title Films.

11
00:59:42,857 --> 00:59:48,857
It stars Cate Blanchett in the title role and is a loose but fact-based portrayal of events during the
latter part of the reign of Elizabeth I, forming a sequel to Kapur's 1998 film Elizabeth.

12
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
The film co-stars Geoffrey Rush (reprising his role from the previous film),
Clive Owen, Jordi Mollà, Abbie Cornish, and Samantha Morton.

13
01:10:34,285 --> 01:10:40,285
The screenplay was written by William Nicholson and Michael Hirst,
and the score composed by Craig Armstrong and A.

14
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Guy Hendrix Dyas was the film's production designer and co-visual effects
supervisor, and the costumes were created by Alexandra Byrne.

15
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
The film was shot at Shepperton Studios and locations around the United Kingdom.

16
01:26:51,428 --> 01:26:57,428
The film premiered on 9 September 2007 at the
Toronto International Film Festival.

17
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
It opened in wide release in the United States on 12 October 2007, premiered in London on 23 October 2007,
and opened wide on 2 November 2007 throughout the rest of the UK and Republic of Ireland.

18
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
At the 80th Academy Awards, the film won Best Costume Design and
Blanchett received a nomination for Best Actress.

19
01:43:08,571 --> 01:43:14,571
The film explores themes of assassination, england,
queen elizabeth i, religious war, tudor.

20
01:48:34,285 --> 01:48:40,285
The tone is emotional.
